cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its results, please cite the work below."
type: software
title: "Reconstruction-independent moment tests for quantum-computed dynamical spectra"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bonilla Vargas"
    given-names: "Nicolás"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6155-4391"
    affiliation: "Universidad Nacional de Colombia"
    email: "ngbonillav@unal.edu.co"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicolasbonilla/reconstruction-independent-moment-tests"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a reconstruction-independent, necessary-condition screen for sample-based
  quantum spectral functions. Low-order spectral moments (m0, m1, m2, and m-1 on open chains) are
  evaluated as ground-state operator expectations, never read back off the reconstructed A(w), and
  compared with the moments of A(w). In a blinded, hash-sealed simulation (300 instances) the sealed
  primary endpoint was a detection rate of 53.7% (101/188; Wilson 95% [46.6, 60.7]%) at a
  false-positive rate of 0.9% (1/112): all determinant truncations (56/56), 45/61 spurious features
  and no under-converged Krylov reconstruction (0/71) were caught. On IBM Heron (ibm_fez) the device
  supplies only the sampled support; no moment is estimated on hardware. The discriminating
  off-diagonal moments are simulation-only, and a sealed on-device n_k experiment was gate-negative
  at current two-qubit error and was not run. No quantum advantage is claimed.
